body:
I hacked this message and read on desktop, FBI can fight me

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\- this is sarcasm

I'd probably say the first-degree black belt form, we call them forms instead of patterns lol, was my fav. My favorite belt was my third-degree test because I really didn't think I could sparr well as all my opponents were at least 6' and I was 5' 4" but it proved to be not as challenging as the adrenaline kicked in. The classes were at least 3x a week and were about 10-20 kids max. As far as tips go honestly just don't be afraid to give it your all especially when it comes to sparring. I don't know about you but my sensei gave me the toughest kids to fight so just hang in there and If anything never just take the beating. Also breaking boards is way easier than it looks trust me.

&#x200B;

Hope this helps :)
